#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199155} :activity/id #uuid "f0143329-4451-5fa5-a3d6-547309257048" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049906 :topic/id #uuid "1ccf84a3-137c-5338-aa7d-bcdca655fa75" :topic/math-academy-id 4396} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199155 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199565 :tutorial/content "The **minimum** of a set $S$ is the element $x_{\\min} \\in S$ such that \n\n$$\nx_{\\min} \\leq x\n$$\n\nfor all $x \\in S.$ In other words, the minimum is the element of $S$ that is *smaller than or equal to* any other element.\n\nSimilarly, the **maximum** of a set $S$ is the element $x_{\\max} \\in S$ such that \n\n$$\nx \\leq x_{\\max}\n$$\n\nfor all $x \\in S.$ In other words, the maximum is the element of $S$ that is *larger than or equal to* any other element.\n\nFor example, what are the minimum and maximum of the following set? \n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{ 2, \\: -\\sqrt{5}, \\: 3, \\: -1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nNote that $-\\sqrt{5} \\approx -2.236.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}min(A) & =min{2,\\,-\\sqrt{5},\\,3,\\,-1}=-\\sqrt{5} \\\\ max(A) & =max{2,\\,-\\sqrt{5},\\,3,\\,-1}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSome sets may not have a maximum or minimum. \n\nFor example, consider the semi-open interval of real numbers $B=[1, 5).$ In this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\min(B) = \\min[1, 5) = 1.\n$$\n\nHowever, since $5 \\notin B,$ the set has no maximum!\n\nFinally, note the following:\n\n- The maximum and minimum elements *must* belong to the underlying set.\n\n- If the maximum or minimum elements exist, they are unique. In other words, there can be, at most, only one maximum and only one minimum.\n\n- If the \"less than or equal to\" operation is not defined *for all* elements of a set $S,$ then the set has no maximum or minimum. For example, the following set has no minimum and maximum:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{\\mathbb R, \\clubsuit, 2, 3, \\langle 1, 2, 3\\rangle \\big\\}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "9377b093-e187-5c5e-9f3d-768297aaf57e" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8236 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "dc18f60a-72ad-5caa-8d0b-2f93237f062b" :step/math-academy-id 157009 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199156}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199156 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198312 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198173 :question/id #uuid "b817524b-bf24-5f11-a0c8-d544f026b0b8" :question/math-academy-id "e-13188"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64180fa2-2268-5954-aadb-2982a2d7a224" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049071} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049168}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198801} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198802} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406786} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406789}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Maximum and Minimum of a Set"} :step/id #uuid "fba9bd9e-ecd9-5f77-8165-270f2b04d324" :step/math-academy-id 157010 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199157}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199157 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198313 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198176 :question/id #uuid "2bf6f02e-e7af-5b94-880d-6f1760a666ec" :question/math-academy-id "e-13194"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f45befc-412b-58aa-8901-d10e63858b52" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050307}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198806} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198807} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406787}] :knowledge-point/title "Explaining the Existence of a Maximum or Minimum"} :step/id #uuid "27fd9c6a-fd4e-5504-b864-7b6a6a143f38" :step/math-academy-id 157013 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199158}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199158 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198314 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198174 :question/id #uuid "cf3362e1-4d5b-5cb4-bcef-523f9927044b" :question/math-academy-id "e-13189"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8ed1932-b363-5a07-a816-93f3078cb801" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050041}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198804} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198805} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406788}] :knowledge-point/title "Maximums and Minimums in More Complex Settings"} :step/id #uuid "26848301-cf0c-5a97-91bd-222dc4cf5583" :step/math-academy-id 157016}] :activity/title "The Maximum and Minimum of a Set" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186198542}]}
